# Rain of Filth gives "Sacrifice this land: Add {B}." to the lands its controller has as it resolves, until end of turn:
# an Island is sacrificed for {B} (the ability does not care about the land's type); Bot2's Forest did not gain it
# (refusal beside Bot1's own land, the positive control); and on Bot1's next turn the effect is gone, so the remaining
# Island cannot be sacrificed (refusal).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Island
Island
Rain of Filth
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Forest x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Rain of Filth.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate(Ability: Sacrifice)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate(Ability: Sacrifice)
? Bot1.Mana = {B}
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate(Ability: Sacrifice)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Island
Bot1.Graveyard = Island; Rain of Filth
